# {{ ansible_managed }}
# SOCKS Proxy Client Configuration
# Generated from: {{ role_path }}/templates/socks_client_config.txt.j2

===========================================
SOCKS PROXY CLIENT CONFIGURATION
===========================================

Proxy Information:
- Server: {{ anon_socks_bind_address }}
- Port: {{ anon_socks_port }}
- Type: SOCKS5
- Authentication: None (if supported)

===========================================
BROWSER CONFIGURATION
===========================================

Firefox:
1. Open Firefox preferences
2. Go to Network Settings
3. Select "Manual proxy configuration"
4. Enter SOCKS Host: {{ anon_socks_bind_address }}
5. Enter Port: {{ anon_socks_port }}
6. Select "SOCKS v5"
7. Check "Proxy DNS when using SOCKS v5"

Chrome/Chromium:
1. Install "Proxy SwitchyOmega" extension
2. Create new profile
3. Set SOCKS proxy to {{ anon_socks_bind_address }}:{{ anon_socks_port }}
4. Select "SOCKS5" protocol

Safari:
1. Open System Preferences > Network
2. Select your network connection
3. Click "Advanced" > "Proxies"
4. Check "SOCKS Proxy"
5. Enter {{ anon_socks_bind_address }}:{{ anon_socks_port }}

===========================================
SYSTEM CONFIGURATION
===========================================

Linux (using environment variables):
export http_proxy=socks5://{{ anon_socks_bind_address }}:{{ anon_socks_port }}
export https_proxy=socks5://{{ anon_socks_bind_address }}:{{ anon_socks_port }}
export all_proxy=socks5://{{ anon_socks_bind_address }}:{{ anon_socks_port }}

Windows (using netsh):
netsh winhttp set proxy proxy-server="socks={{ anon_socks_bind_address }}:{{ anon_socks_port }}"

macOS (using networksetup):
networksetup -setsocksfirewallproxy "Wi-Fi" {{ anon_socks_bind_address }} {{ anon_socks_port }}

===========================================
APPLICATION CONFIGURATION
===========================================

curl:
curl --socks5 {{ anon_socks_bind_address }}:{{ anon_socks_port }} https://httpbin.org/ip

wget:
wget --proxy=on --socks5={{ anon_socks_bind_address }}:{{ anon_socks_port }} https://httpbin.org/ip

git:
git config --global http.proxy socks5://{{ anon_socks_bind_address }}:{{ anon_socks_port }}

===========================================
TESTING CONNECTION
===========================================

Run the test script:
{{ anon_socks_client_config_path }}/test-proxy.sh

Or test manually:
curl --socks5 {{ anon_socks_bind_address }}:{{ anon_socks_port }} https://httpbin.org/ip

Expected result: Your public IP address should be different from your local IP.

===========================================
TROUBLESHOOTING
===========================================

Common issues:
1. Connection refused: Check if SOCKS proxy is running
2. Timeout: Check firewall settings
3. DNS issues: Enable "Proxy DNS" in browser settings
4. Application not working: Some apps don't support SOCKS5

For support, check the logs:
docker logs {{ anon_container_name | default('anon-relay') }}

